1
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:59,333
The Flying Sailor is a animation, comedy, fantasy
film directed by Amanda Forbis.

2
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:52,666
The Flying Sailor is based on the Halifax Explosion of 1917 when two ships collided in
the Halifax Harbour causing the largest accidental explosion in history.

3
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Among the tragic stories of the disaster is the remarkable account of a sailor who, blown skyward from the deck of a
British cargo steamer, flew over 2 km before landing completely unharmed, but naked except for his boots.

4
00:03:33,333 --> 00:03:39,333
The Flying Sailor is a 2022 Canadian independent animated short film directed
by Oscar-nominated directors Wendy Tilby and Amanda Forbis.

5
00:04:26,666 --> 00:04:32,666
The film debuted at the 2022 Annecy International Animation Film Festival and has received several nominations and awards, including a nomination for Best
Animated Short Film at the 95th Academy Awards, and winning the award for the Best Canadian Film at the Ottawa International Animation Festival.

6
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
The film was named to the Toronto International Film Festival's
annual year-end Canada's Top Ten list for 2022.

7
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:19,333
The film explores themes of based on true story, halifax
explosion, hand drawn animation, short film.

8
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:12,666
The tone is lighthearted.
